              "review_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XFZRVnP-MTU&t=274s",
              "start_seconds": 274,
              "end_seconds": 402,
              "label": "Creating a Figure and one Axes explicitly with plt.subplots()",
              "summary": "The presenter recaps that the Figure is the container holding all plots — the whole window — and that Axes are the actual plots inside it, with a Figure able to hold more than one. They then introduce the object-oriented approach: writing fig, ax = plt.subplots() instantiates both a Figure and an Axes at once. Because no row or column count is passed, subplots defaults to a one-by-one grid, producing exactly one Axes assigned to ax.",
