          "block_id": "tile_viz_figures_layout_plotting.r01.b01",
          "role": "definition",
          "text": "The Figure is the outer canvas — the whole window. The Axes is the inner plotting area where data is drawn. `fig, ax = plt.subplots()` creates both at once: `fig` is the canvas, `ax` is the plotting area. Plotting calls like `ax.plot(x, y)` go on `ax`, never on `fig`.",
