          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_viz_figures_layout_plotting.r03.b01",
          "role": "syntax",
          "text": "`plt.plot([18, 22, 26, 19, 30])` uses one argument: the list is treated as y-values and x-positions are filled in automatically starting at 0 (so 0, 1, 2, 3, 4). `plt.plot([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [18, 22, 26, 19, 30])` uses two arguments: the first list sets the x-axis to 1–5, the second sets the y-axis. Both calls produce a line; only the x-axis differs.",
